export default {"T000981":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"equivalence\" data-relation-style=\"equivalence\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Equivalence</span><h3>Flat ∧ Local complete intersection ⇔ Syntomic</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Left conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000006\"><span>Flat</span><code>P000006</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000008\"><span>Local complete intersection</span><code>P000008</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T000981\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000981</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇔</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Right conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000005\"><span>Syntomic</span><code>P000005</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> For the converse, flatness with a Koszul-regular factorization gives local finite presentation and local complete intersection fibres. For the forward direction, standard syntomic presentations supply Koszul-regular factorizations.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/069K\">Stacks 069K · syntomic if and only if flat and local complete intersection · Stacks 069K · numbered source statement</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/more-morphisms/#tag-069K\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-658-43031-3_4\">U. Görtz and T. Wedhorn, Algebraic Geometry II, Definition 19.51 and Proposition 19.52(i)–(ii), flatness and the fibre criterion</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000981\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T000981\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000982":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"equivalence\" data-relation-style=\"equivalence\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Equivalence</span><h3>Smooth ∧ Unramified ⇔ Étale</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Left conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000004\"><span>Smooth</span><code>P000004</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000007\"><span>Unramified</span><code>P000007</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T000982\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000982</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇔</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Right conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000003\"><span>Étale</span><code>P000003</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> The equivalence holds at every source point and gives the stated equivalence for the morphism.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02GK\">Stacks 02GK · étale if and only if smooth and unramified</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-02GK\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000982\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T000982\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000983":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"equivalence\" data-relation-style=\"equivalence\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Equivalence</span><h3>Quasi-coherent module on a crystalline site ⇔ Objectwise quasi-coherent crystalline module ∧ Crystal in modules</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Left conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000510\"><span>Quasi-coherent module on a crystalline site</span><code>P000510</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T000983\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000983</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇔</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Right conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000509\"><span>Objectwise quasi-coherent crystalline module</span><code>P000509</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#G000048\"><span>Crystal in modules</span><code>G000048</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Sites and presentations</p><p><strong>Hypotheses.</strong> A sheaf of modules over the crystalline structure sheaf on the small or big crystalline site, in Stacks Situation 60.7.5.</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> A presentation on each covering slice gives a presentation on its thickening and pulls back to the same presentation on each source thickening. Conversely, work on a slice whose thickening is affine. Choose a presentation there and use the crystal base-change isomorphisms to pull it back throughout the slice.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07IT\">Stacks 07IT · original numbered result</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/crystalline/#tag-07IT\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000983\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T000983\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000984":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"equivalence\" data-relation-style=\"equivalence\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Equivalence</span><h3>Objectwise quasi-coherent crystalline module ∧ Crystal in modules ⇔ Crystal in quasi-coherent modules</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Left conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000509\"><span>Objectwise quasi-coherent crystalline module</span><code>P000509</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#G000048\"><span>Crystal in modules</span><code>G000048</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T000984\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000984</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇔</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Right conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000512\"><span>Crystal in quasi-coherent modules</span><code>P000512</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Sites and presentations</p><p><strong>Hypotheses.</strong> A sheaf of modules over the crystalline structure sheaf on the small or big crystalline site, in Stacks Situation 60.7.5.</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> These are the two conditions in the quasi-coherent crystal criterion.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07IU\">Stacks 07IU · original numbered result</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/crystalline/#tag-07IU\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000984\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T000984\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000985":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"equivalence\" data-relation-style=\"equivalence\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Equivalence</span><h3>Crystal in quasi-coherent modules ∧ Finite locally free module on a crystalline site ⇔ Crystal in finite locally free modules</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Left conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000512\"><span>Crystal in quasi-coherent modules</span><code>P000512</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000511\"><span>Finite locally free module on a crystalline site</span><code>P000511</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T000985\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000985</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇔</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Right conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000513\"><span>Crystal in finite locally free modules</span><code>P000513</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Sites and presentations</p><p><strong>Hypotheses.</strong> A sheaf of modules over the crystalline structure sheaf on the small or big crystalline site, in Stacks Situation 60.7.5.</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Finite local freeness on the site is the additional defining condition.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07IU\">Stacks 07IU · original numbered result</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/crystalline/#tag-07IU\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000985\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T000985\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000986":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Finite locally free module on a crystalline site ⇒ Quasi-coherent module on a crystalline site</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000511\"><span>Finite locally free module on a crystalline site</span><code>P000511</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T000986\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000986</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000510\"><span>Quasi-coherent module on a crystalline site</span><code>P000510</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Sites and presentations</p><p><strong>Hypotheses.</strong> A sheaf of modules over the crystalline structure sheaf on the small or big crystalline site, in Stacks Situation 60.7.5.</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> On each slice on which the module is finite free, the chosen trivialization supplies a free presentation.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DL\">Stacks 03DL · original numbered result</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites-modules/#tag-03DL\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000986\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T000986\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>"};
